==English==

===Etymology 1===
From obsolete {{bor|en|fr|rebuffer}}, from {{der|en|frm|rebuffer}} (compare {{ncog|fr|rebiffer|t=to rise up, revolt}}), from {{der|en|it|ribuffare}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/ɹɪˈbʌf/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-rebuff1.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌf|s=2}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A sudden [[resistance]] or [[refusal]].
#: {{ux|en|He was surprised by her quick '''rebuff''' to his proposal.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1986|author=w:John le Carré|title=w:A Perfect Spy| passage= And it is symptomatic of the many paradoxes of Lederer's life that of all the people in the room, Brotherhood is the one whom he would most wish to serve, if ever he had the opportunity, even though — or perhaps because — his occasional efforts to ingratiate himself with his adopted hero have met with iron '''rebuff'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Stephen Collinson|title=Michigan vaccine rebuff puts Biden and a top ally in a dicey political spot|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2021/04/13/politics/michigan-joe-biden-gretchen-whitmer-covid-19/index.html|date=2021-04-13|passage=His administration’s blunt '''rebuff''' of a plea by his ally and Michigan’s Democratic Gov. Gretchen Whitmer for an increased supply of vaccines to combat a Covid-19 spike represents the kind of tough decision the President and his team will increasingly face on the exit road from the crisis.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Reuters|title=US, Brazil float new Venezuela election despite government, opposition rebuffs|magazine=w:Fox News|url=https://www.foxnews.com/world/us-brazil-float-new-venezuela-election-despite-government-opposition-rebuffs|date=2024-08-15|passage=U.S. President Joe Biden said on Thursday that he would support a new election in Venezuela, after Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva also floated the idea, despite '''rebuffs''' from Venezuela's ruling party and its opposition which both claim victory in the July 28 contest.}}
# Repercussion, or beating back.
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=2|passage=the strong '''rebuff''' of some tumultuous cloud|year=1873}}

